{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\nThe reconciler multi-project fan-out (story 1734) runs every mapped project's base\n(active + done-recent) JQL queries in a single flat loop with NO per-project error\nisolation: `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/fetcher.py` `_build_snapshot` builds\n`queries` across all projects and iterates `for jql, cap in queries:` — any single\nproject's transport failure (ACLI 400 unknown-project, 401/403 permission, 404,\n429 rate-limit, 5xx, timeout) propagates out and ABORTS THE ENTIRE PASS for all\nprojects. The enrichment loop directly below already fails open per-project\n(`_enrich_project` \"each pass failing open independently so a per-project fault\ndegrades only that project\"). The base-query loop never inherited that resilience.\n\nThis is the PROVEN root cause of the 2026-08-15 production outage (bug\n05b8-4efe-8d58-4c27): a single mapped-but-nonexistent project key (`LEG`) —\nsyntactically valid, so `_validate_project_key` passes — made ACLI exit 1 and took\ndown ~12h of scheduled Reconcile Bridge passes across every project.\n\n## Approach\nWrap each project's base-query fetch in a per-project boundary that mirrors the\nenrichment loop's fail-open contract: on a per-project transport error, SKIP that\nproject (do not merge partial results that would look like deletions), emit an\nobservable alert via `alert_store.append({\"kind\": \"fetcher-project-fetch-failed\",\n\"project\": <key>, \"pass_id\": pass_id, ...})`, and CONTINUE to the other projects.\nPreserve the existing fail-CLOSED behavior for a syntactically-invalid/absent key\n(that still raises in `jql_active` — bug 626d intent is unchanged) and for a\n`BackendPaginationStallError` (a stalled pager is a truncated whole-project read and\nmust still surface), matching the enrichment loop's exception handling exactly.\nRestructure the flat `queries` tuple so the try/except is scoped PER PROJECT (both\nthe active and done-recent query for a project share the boundary); keep the dedup\n(`seen_keys`) and the `fetcher-dedup-suppressed` alert behavior intact.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] One mapped project's base-query transport error does not abort the pass; the other projects' issues still land in the snapshot. Verified by the new unit `test_one_project_base_query_failure_does_not_abort_pass` in `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetch_multi_project.py`.\n- [ ] A per-project base-query fetch failure emits an observable `fetcher-project-fetch-failed` alert naming the project and pass_id. Verified: the new unit asserts a matching record in `bridge_state/bridge_alerts/*.jsonl`.\n- [ ] The single-project (unseeded store) path remains regression-identical. Verified: the existing `test_single_project_fallback_is_regression_identical` still passes.\n- [ ] A syntactically-invalid/absent key still fails closed (626d preserved) and a `BackendPaginationStallError` still re-raises. Verified: `_validate_project_key` is still called by `jql_active` outside the per-project try, and the boundary re-raises `BackendPaginationStallError` exactly as `_enrich_project` does.\n\n## Testing\nAdd an always-on unit (no live Jira) to `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetch_multi_project.py`\nusing a `_FakeClient` whose `search_issues` RAISES for project `BAD` (e.g. an\n`HTTPError`/ACLI error) but returns issues for `OK`; assert `OK`'s issues land in\nthe snapshot, the pass is not aborted, and the `fetcher-project-fetch-failed` alert\nfired for `BAD`. This is the always-on regression the incident lacked (closes the\nP0-3 test gap). Mutation check: reverting the per-project try/except returns the\ntest to RED. Run with\n`python -m pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetch_multi_project.py -q`,\nplus `make lint` and `make typecheck`.\n\n## Sequencing\nEdits `fetcher.py` `_build_snapshot` base-query region. Ticket C (non-Done status)\nalso edits `fetcher.py` — C is sequenced AFTER this ticket to avoid conflict."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786808687990103001,"uuid":"1e84733b-4d5c-46e9-bec6-2eee3ffe89f6"}